  "notes": [
    "`time` read in seconds, from `GPS Time of Week`: it counts milliseconds, below a week's 604,800,000, and climbs by a median of 1000.0 per unit of its `time`",
    "`pressure` read in pascals, from the values: its first sample, on the pad, is 98358, a launch site's pressure in pascals (50,000 to 110,000 Pa)",
    "`Pressure MSL` and `Pressure AGL` read in meters, from the pressure: from the first sample to the one of lowest pressure, the standard atmosphere climbs 543.4 m and the column 543.4 meters",
    "`GPS MSL` read in meters, assumed: as the barometric altitudes, the software setting one unit system for its displays (p33)",
    "`temperature` read in degrees Celsius, assumed: the manual's sensor reads °C or °F (p25), and the software sets one unit system for its displays (p33), here the altitudes' meters",
    "`acceleration`, `lat. X accel.` and `lat. Y accel.` read in g, from the manual: it plots the accelerations \"in G's\", the long axis's with gravity in it (p23–24)",
    "`Gyro X`, `Gyro Y` and `Gyro Z` read in degrees per second, from the manual: \"degrees/sec\" (p24)",
    "`eject. bat. voltage` read in volts, assumed: the manual plots the batteries' and the four lines' voltages without naming a unit (p24)",
    "`comp. bat. voltage` read in volts, assumed: the manual plots the batteries' and the four lines' voltages without naming a unit (p24)",
    "`A Voltage` read in volts, assumed: the manual plots the batteries' and the four lines' voltages without naming a unit (p24)",
    "`lat` and `long` read in degrees, from the values: decimal numbers, as the manual's sample export writes them (Table 2, p40)",
    "`Mag X`, `Mag Y` and `Mag Z` kept as written, in a unit no source bears out: the manual gives tesla (p24), but the field the sample files' columns make, 0.0011 to 0.0022, is 20 to 40 times the Earth's, and the record has no quantity for a magnetic field",
    "`GPS Time of Week` kept as written, in milliseconds: the record has no quantity for a time of the GPS week",
    "24 rows, the first on line 8, write the run-out GPS group, `time,lat,…`, one empty cell too wide: the cell after it was dropped, so that the groups to its right are read under their names"
  ]
